Z||000000||87 Steve GT||01-30-2000||09:29 AM||||Hey everyone.... my 87 GT(auto) will only idle for about 20-30 sec. then my car has started a real fast jerking (2-3) times then just dies.....  My question is .... could my fuel filter be bad or have some junk in it, OR well im just idling (LOWER??? FUEL PRESS&gt; ) is that not enough pressure to BLOW through my possibly bad fuel filter?????  Did any of that make sense??? ANY input would be greatly be helpful.... Steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wrench||01-30-2000||09:38 AM||||After it dies can you restart and then drive off? To verify your fuel system is real easy. Just have someone put a pressure gauge on the schrader valve then start the car. You should maintain 45+ psi of pressure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87 Steve GT||01-30-2000||09:54 AM||||YES IT'LL RESTART oopppps  sorry not really yelling... lol  just wont idle for long..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||01-30-2000||11:09 AM||||Check the tps.  Also it might be time for a good De-carbonizing.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||01-30-2000||01:42 PM||||You need to put a guage on that fuel rail,and watch the pressure as the engine dies in order to determine if it's in the plumbing,or electric controls.Then ,if it's losing pressure,begin to check the fuel pump,filter.If it's got pressure the whole time,then there are some other things to check.  <BR>Good luck ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick||01-30-2000||03:22 PM||||<BR>If it was a fuel supply problem, I don't understand why it would ONLY affect the ability to idle. This might occur with a worn mechanical fuel pump, but I doubt anything similar would happen with an electric one.<P>I would guess the problem is elsewhere.||||reg||5
Z||000006||David Gamache||01-31-2000||03:13 PM||||If you check the service manual(haynes etc)your problem sounds like a faulty torque converter clutch (TCC) on your auto trans. This when failed will cause the car to stall.<BR>reciently in this forum someone discussed the steps to replace this part. You may want to locate that discussion.||||reg||1
